  "body": {
    "id": "lem:dai-visible-selectedness",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(\\eta\\in\\mathfrak M_{D,K}^{\\mathrm{Dai}}\\), with \\(\\mathcal O=\\mathcal O(\\eta)\\) formed from the faithful pooled selected laws \\(P_{\\eta,k}^{\\mathrm{pool}}\\), if \\(uv\\) is absent from the observational skeleton \\(H\\) and present in an observed intervention-regime skeleton, then \\(u,v\\in A(\\eta)\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "O",
      "M_DK",
      "D",
      "K",
      "V",
      "H",
      "A",
      "eta",
      "P_pool"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:selection-structure",
      "ass:selection-parent-domain",
      "ass:pretreatment-selection",
      "def:model-class",
      "def:oracle-signature",
      "lem:dai-twin-mag-interface"
    ],
    "justification": "Dai et al.'s Lemma 4 supplies the initial visible-selectedness certificate used by the rule handle.",
    "gap": "Dai et al., Lemma 4 on p. 6, is the published source of this intervention-created-adjacency certificate; the closure of partially certified selection membership is not part of that lemma.",
    "consumer": "It initializes cross-regime selectedness without analyst-supplied labels.",
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(uv\\) be absent from \\(H\\) and present in the regime-\\(k\\) skeleton.  The regime-adjacency equivalence in \\(\\mathrm{lem:dai\\mbox{-}twin\\mbox{-}mag\\mbox{-}interface}\\) rules out its observational-adjacency alternative.  It therefore supplies an \\(H\\)-path from \\(u\\) to \\(v\\) whose endpoints and internal vertices are all in \\(A(\\eta)\\), with every internal vertex affected in regime \\(k\\).  In particular,\n\\[\nu\\in A(\\eta),\\qquad v\\in A(\\eta).\n\\]\nThe source lemma is graphical, so no positivity, rank, conditioning denominator, or limiting argument enters this implication. \\(\\square\\)",
